descriptionText:
Company Name: Evomaton Private Limited, Bangalore, India.
Experience: 2+ years
Job mode: Hybrid, 4 days/week from the office in Bangalore.
About Evomaton:
Evomaton is a consulting and software services company providing services for AI/ML/Data/IoT and other high-end digital systems in EPC, Mobility, Healthcare, and Product Engineering domains. Data acquisition, synthetic data, data architecture, data pipelining, big data, prescriptive analytics, ML/DL/GenAI/ Agentic, and MLOps for various digital domains from core engineering to electronics products are the areas of operation for Evomaton.
Company Website: www.evomaton.com
Job Description:
We are seeking a highly knowledgeable and experienced Mechanical/Chemical engineer with 2-4 years of experience in the engineering industry - EPC/ Engineering Services / AEC/ Engineering Products doing design activities.&nbsp;The person should be interested Engineering AI  and should have done an AI/ML course at least 6 Months.
&nbsp;
Key Responsibilities: As a ML Engineer, you will have the unique opportunity to work on groundbreaking projects, learn from senior technologists, and experience rapid career growth in a collaborative environment.&nbsp;You will be initially responsible for testing and validation of Engineering AI solutions and will transition into ML engineer role within a year.&nbsp;&nbsp;You will learn LLM/ Classic ML/Image processing applications, lifecycle process, eval techniques,&nbsp;engineering confidence, harnesses and context techniques for modelling engineering problems.&nbsp;&nbsp;


-EDA and Requirement engineering for Engineering AI Problems&nbsp;
-Design the eval systems and Test Harnesses for Engineering AI .
-Testing P&amp;ID, GA, and isometric drawing-based AI applications
-Develop and implement advanced prompt engineering techniques for Unit and System testing
-Development of simulators and test code&nbsp;
-Participation in feasibility and POC&nbsp;as you develop the maturity


Qualification&nbsp;
Bachelor or master’s in engineering in Mechanical or Chemical Engineering&nbsp;
&nbsp;Work experience in design and development of engineering systems&nbsp;
Good knowledge in drawing and other engineering representations&nbsp;
Sound Technical background and capability of problem-solving&nbsp;
At least 6 months of AI/ML study through formal courses&nbsp;
Work experience in AI/ML teams, even as an intern will be a big plus&nbsp;


Why Join Us?
· Be part of a early team of a Startup  in a promising AI/ML startup with significant growth potential.
.&nbsp;Learn various techniques of Engineering AI and Physical AI from experience team&nbsp;
· Learn Classic ML/DL/LLM RAG/Agentic AI on the job.
· Work on bleeding-edge LLM and Generative AI projects that are pushing the boundaries Engineering AI
